  "notes": [
    "Rows 5-6 are static West 72 letterhead (Buyer/Signator/address boilerplate) -- left untouched, no field binding.",
    "Header context (venue address/capacity, agency, agent, phone, email, billing, lineup) comes from the linked Offer via settlement.offer_id, looked up live at export time. Blank when no offer is linked.",
    "I8 ('Date:') binds to event_date_label -- 'MA' in the source example was confirmed a stray data-entry mistake, not a real field.",
    "The sheet's ORDERS column (J) has no backing field on the real Settlement type -- cc_fees is already a single real aggregate, pro-rated across tiers by sold count (same as the existing PDF adapter). ORDERS column is dropped from the generated layout.",
    "fixed_expenses / variable_expenses / ticket_audit are true repeating sections -- both label and value are data-driven per row, not fixed category names. Template's current rows serve as the style stencil + example row count.",
    "show_lineup is capped at 3 fixed lines (B12/B13/B14) rather than a true repeating section -- row 12 shares physical space with the unrelated Email: field, so structural row-insertion there would corrupt the header layout. Entries beyond 3 are dropped for now."
  ],
